    <item>
      <title>Oil Market Fragmentation Is Making Crude Both Cheap and Expensive</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-22/oil-market-fragmentation-is-making-crude-both-cheap-and-expensive</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">6784c3d6b72c3c6c4a202717</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 03:00:27 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>With oil, as with real estate, it’s all about location, location, location. The petroleum market has never been truly global, but rather a loosely connected collection of regional sources. When prices diverged, barrels were shuttled to the most lucrative destination. But with freight rates ballooning to prohibitively expensive levels, the region-to-region flow has been disrupted. The result? The the oil market is fragmenting.</description>
      <dc:creator>Javier Blas</dc:creator>
